§§ `ss 201-203 - screening an offender`

-- s 201 illus: A, knowing that B has murdered Z, assists B to hide the body to screen
-- B.
`s 201 illus` MEANS `Offence Information Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `the particulars`
    `knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed` IS TRUE
    `causes any evidence of the commission of that offence to disappear` IS TRUE
    `gives any information respecting the offence which he knows or believes to be false` IS FALSE
    `with the intention of screening the offender from legal punishment` IS TRUE
    `intentionally omits to give any information respecting that offence` IS FALSE
    `which he is legally bound to give` IS FALSE
    `the offence is punishable with death` IS TRUE
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years` IS FALSE
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for any term not extending to 20 years` IS FALSE
    `the offence` IS "murder"
    `what was done` IS "by assisting B to hide the body of Z"

-- s 201 illus: "A is liable to imprisonment for 10 years, and also to fine."
#ASSERT `offence under s 201` `s 201 illus`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 201` `s 201 illus`)'s punishment EQUALS "imprisonment for a term which may extend to 10 years, and shall also be liable to fine"
#ASSERT (`punishment prescribed by s 201(a)`)'s `maximum term in months` EQUALS JUST 120
#ASSERT (`punishment prescribed by s 201(a)`)'s fine EQUALS `shall also be liable to`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 201` `s 201 illus`)'s text EQUALS "You, Tan Ah Kow, are charged that you, on or about the 1st day of June 2026, at about 10.00 am, at the State Courts, 1 Havelock Square, Singapore, knowing or having reason to believe that an offence, namely murder, had been committed, did cause evidence of the commission of that offence to disappear, or give information respecting it which you knew or believed to be false, with the intention of screening the offender from legal punishment, to wit, by assisting B to hide the body of Z, and you have thereby committed an offence punishable under section 201 of the Penal Code 1871."
-- s 201 (a)-(c): one-fourth of the longest term (theft, s 379: 3 years = 36 months -> 9 months)
#ASSERT `one-fourth part of the longest term of imprisonment` 36 EQUALS 9

-- FORK JO-3: the screened offence's punishment is unknown, so no paragraph of s 201
-- prescribes a punishment and the charge refuses.
`s 201 without a tier` MEANS `Offence Information Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `the particulars`
    `knowing or having reason to believe that an offence has been committed` IS TRUE
    `causes any evidence of the commission of that offence to disappear` IS TRUE
    `gives any information respecting the offence which he knows or believes to be false` IS FALSE
    `with the intention of screening the offender from legal punishment` IS TRUE
    `intentionally omits to give any information respecting that offence` IS FALSE
    `which he is legally bound to give` IS FALSE
    `the offence is punishable with death` IS FALSE
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for life or with imprisonment which may extend to 20 years` IS FALSE
    `the offence is punishable with imprisonment for any term not extending to 20 years` IS FALSE
    `the offence` IS ""
    `what was done` IS ""

#ASSERT `causes disappearance of evidence of an offence to screen the offender` `s 201 without a tier`
#ASSERT NOT `offence under s 201` `s 201 without a tier`
#ASSERT (`charge under s 201` `s 201 without a tier`)'s refusal EQUALS "A charge under section 201 would assert that the facts fulfil every legal condition of causing disappearance of evidence of an offence committed, or giving false information touching it, to screen the offender (CPC s 123(5)). On the facts given they do not: the offence is punishable with death, with imprisonment for life or up to 20 years, or where it is punishable with imprisonment for any term not extending to 20 years."

§§ `s 204A - perverting the course of justice`

`s 204A Explanation 1` MEANS `Course of Justice Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `the particulars`
    `does an act that has a tendency to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice` IS TRUE
    `knowing that the act is likely to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice` IS FALSE
    `intending to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice` IS TRUE
    `the act is a mere warning to a witness that he may be prosecuted for perjury if he gives false evidence` IS TRUE
    `what was done` IS ""

-- s 204A Explanation 2: a person sentenced to imprisonment leaves Singapore unlawfully
-- to avoid serving it.
`s 204A Explanation 2` MEANS `Course of Justice Facts` WITH
    particulars IS `the particulars`
    `does an act that has a tendency to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice` IS TRUE
    `knowing that the act is likely to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice` IS FALSE
    `intending to obstruct, prevent, pervert or defeat the course of justice` IS TRUE
    `the act is a mere warning to a witness that he may be prosecuted for perjury if he gives false evidence` IS FALSE
